{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let's evaluate the two sigma expressions and see which of them results in $2+5+8+11$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^4(3n-1)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=[3(1)-1]+[3(2)-1]+[3(3)-1]+[3(4)-1]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2+5+8+11\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=0}^3(2+3n)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=[2+3(0)]+[2+3(1)]+[2+3(2)]+[2+3(3)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2+5+8+11\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, both $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^4(3n-1)$ and $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=0}^3(2+3n)$ are equal to $2+5+8+11$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Consider the sum $2+5+8+11$.\n\n**Which expression is equal to the above sum?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^4(3n-1)$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=0}^3(2+3n)$","correct":true},{"isNoneOfTheAbove":true}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":true,"multipleSelect":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
